<div class="card en" lang="en">
<h2>English — School PDF privacy practices</h2>
<p><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:{{ config('schoolpdf.support_email') }}">{{ config('schoolpdf.support_email') }}</a>. School PDF does not offer student account registration or login.</p>
<p><strong>Local content:</strong> The student's name, class, level, subjects, selected images and generated PDFs are stored on the device. Creating a PDF does not upload these files to School PDF servers. Sharing or exporting can send a copy to a service you choose, governed by that service's own policy.</p>
<p><strong>Optional adult analytics:</strong> With explicit consent from adults aged 18 or over, the app transmits a randomly generated installation ID, platform, app version, interface language, notification settings and activity timestamp. The server may infer an approximate country through a trusted proxy. No GPS location is requested and the device-registration database does not persist IP addresses.</p>
<p><strong>Notifications and third parties:</strong> Google Firebase Cloud Messaging processes notification-related technical information and tokens when configured. Google Mobile Ads SDK is present in the code; production ad rendering is disabled by default unless explicitly enabled in a compliant build. Third-party SDKs may process device identifiers and technical information according to their policies and the build configuration. Student names, homework photos and PDFs are not used for ad targeting.</p>
<p><strong>Security and retention:</strong> The app's own API requests use HTTPS. Device secrets are stored hashed on our backend, while stored FCM tokens are encrypted. Inactive device records become eligible for daily cleanup after 90 days, only when the server scheduler actually runs. Third-party retention may differ.</p>
<p><strong>Deletion:</strong> You can revoke analytics consent and delete an optional server device record within the app. Supported app versions also let you delete the local student profile and generated PDFs. Your gallery originals and exported copies remain outside the app's control. See <a href="{{ url('/data-deletion') }}">School PDF data deletion</a> or email <a href="mailto:{{ config('schoolpdf.support_email') }}">{{ config('schoolpdf.support_email') }}</a> for help. Anonymous installation records may not be identifiable by email alone.</p>
</div></x-shell>
